bolt-sysfs: know Panther Lake's NHIs

bolt reads whether a host's USB4 domain keeps its UUID across reboots
from a table of NHI PCI IDs, and logs a warning for one it doesn't
know before taking it as unstable. Panther Lake's integrated NHIs, like
Ice Lake's and Tiger Lake's, aren't stable, so the answer is already
right and only the warning goes. Upstream's 3a38c237 (after 0.9.11)
adds the same IDs.

diff -ruN a/boltd/bolt-sysfs.c b/boltd/bolt-sysfs.c
--- a/boltd/bolt-sysfs.c
+++ b/boltd/bolt-sysfs.c
@@ -627,6 +627,10 @@
   {0x8a17, FALSE}, // ICL_NHI0
   {0x9a1b, FALSE}, // TGL_NHI0
   {0x9a1d, FALSE}, // TGL_NHI1
+  {0xe333, FALSE}, // PTL_M_NHI0
+  {0xe334, FALSE}, // PTL_M_NHI1
+  {0xe433, FALSE}, // PTL_P_NHI0
+  {0xe434, FALSE}, // PTL_P_NHI1
 };
 
 gboolean
